}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Megaphrodite''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Almighty Aphrodite''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Among the first cat units to have the [[Long Distance]] ability, Aphrodite still offers a very potent sniper kit even to this day. While 3.4K DPS at level 30 is bad on paper, this is more than made up for by her incredible 600 standing range, which is high even compared to other snipers and gives her incredible safety. She also packs a Long Distance that pierces up to 850, allowing her to use stepping stones to safely hit threats that might otherwise be able to attack her, like [[Director Kurosawah]].

Because of this, she does really well at hitting the enemy backliners. She can wear down most bosses or strong units easily, being able to easily snipe long-ranged enemies such as [[Master A.]], [[Camelle]], [[Le'boin]], [[THE SLOTH]] and so on. However, Aphrodite also packs a blind spot of 450, making her more difficult to use against pushers such as [[Bore]]. She is also generally less effective against piercing damage from the likes of [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance Enemies]] and [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|wave attackers]], as they can attack her from afar.

While Aphrodite is already a good generalist thanks to her high range, she also packs [[Massive Damage|Massive Damage]] against [[Alien Enemies]], and as expected, she is a powerhouse against them. 13.6k effective DPS at Lv.30 is no joke, especially for a sniper who stands at 600 range, and this niche has good compatibility as many Aliens are backliners who stand perfectly in Aphrodite's Long Distance, such as [[Calamary]], [[Alpacky]] and [[Elder Sloth]]. With support, even Alien pushers like [[Nimoy Bore]] are not safe from her wrath either. When boosted to Lv.52 or higher and with all Anti-Alien fruit treasures unlocked, Aphrodite even becomes strong enough to brute force through [[UltraBaaBaa]] and [[Youcan]]'s barriers.

Due to her blindspot, Aphrodite pairs well with other attackers and meatshields that can protect her. She works especially well with [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], as he can Slow enemies, especially frontliners, and keep them within Aphrodite's Long Distance, allowing her to hit them consistently. It is worth knowing that her blind spot allows her to cheese certain stages by stalling peons in it and stacking her up, and that her Long Distance's pierce could let her snipe enemy bases in stages like [[Vulcanizer (Deadly)|Vulcanizer]].

==='''True Form'''===
Due to how strong Aphrodite was in the early days of Battle Cats, she was punished with a subpar True Form and Talents.

Almighty Aphrodite brings a mere 19% health boost and nothing else. This makes her not worth the [[Catfruit|Epic Catfruit Seed]] needed for the evolution, and should only be unlocked if you are planning to unlock her Ultra Talents.

==='''Talents'''===
As a sniper, the basic attack boost would help a lot, but what quickly becomes a problem is that Aphrodite doesn't have basic stat boosts. She has 4 resistances and the ability to '''[[Slow|Slow]]'''. Slow would have been a good ability on her, due to her long range and wide Long Distance coverage, but it is hampered by its low proc chance and poor uptime.

Her '''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resistances]]''' to Curse, Weaken and Freeze are also unnecessary, as she has enough range to avoid those altogether. Wave resistance is a different kind of useless, as Aphrodite has health too low to tank many Waves, and [[Wave Shield|Wave Shields]] already exist to block said Waves.

There is no reason to invest NP in her, as nothing complements her whatsoever. Only invest XP, as it's the only way to increase her general damage, which is her best aspect.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Almighty Aphrodite's Ultra Talents finally give her something she had been waiting years for: an increase to her damage output. At Lv.60, both the '''Attack Buff''' and '''Attack Frequency Up''' bring her from a solid 6,418 DPS to a strong 9,630 DPS, or a near 50% increase. This simply makes her better at what she already did well, especially when fighting Aliens, against which she has a colossal ''38,520'' effective DPS.

Of course, however, this comes at a hefty cost of many Dark Catseyes and 450 total NP for both Talents, only exacerbated by the sheer uselessness of her already-costly True Form at base. One may prefer to invest those resources into a unit that improves more drastically from their Ultra Talents, such as [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Amaterasu]] or [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Akuma Hayabusa]], rather than a unit who serves to gain such a meager increase for the level of commitment needed. Should you be willing to get these, however, the power boost Aphrodite recieves is very noticeable and shouldn't be underestimated. If you want to focus on only one to save on NP, go for her TBA reduction, as this gives a higher boost to DPS per level for the same cost as her damage buff and leaves her with a satisfactory 8,025 base DPS.

==='''Talent Orbs''' ===
Aphrodite should get a Massive Damage Orb to enhance her potential against Aliens. One big benefit should you decide to go the extra mile and unlock her Ultra Talents is that she gains a second orb slot. Assuming she equips 2 S Rank Massive Damage orbs, she gains an absurd ''48,150'' effective anti-Alien DPS, being among the best anti-Aliens in the game. Additionally, an S Rank Resist Waves orb can be paired with her Wave Resist Talent from earlier to effectively give her Wave Immunity.

